{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef build_segment_tree(size):\n    tree_size = 1\n    while tree_size < size:\n        tree_size *= 2\n    return [0] * (tree_size * 2)\n\ndef update_segment(tree, index, value):\n    pos = index + len(tree) // 2\n    tree[pos] = value\n    pos //= 2\n    while pos > 0:\n        tree[pos] = tree[pos * 2] + tree[pos * 2 + 1]\n        pos //= 2\n\ndef range_query(tree, left, right):\n    left += len(tree) // 2\n    right += len(tree) // 2\n    total = 0\n    while left <= right:\n        if left % 2 == 1:\n            total += tree[left]\n            left += 1\n        if right % 2 == 0:\n            total += tree[right]\n            right -= 1\n        left //= 2\n        right //= 2\n    return total\n\ndef prime_factors(n):\n    factors = []\n    d = 2\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            factors.append(d)\n            n //= d\n        d += 1\n    if n > 1:\n        factors.append(n)\n    return factors\n\ndef euler_totient(n):\n    factors = set(prime_factors(n))\n    result = n\n    for p in factors:\n        result = result // p * (p - 1)\n    return result\n\ndef modular_product(start, end, modulus):\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(start, end + 1):\n        result = (result * i) % modulus\n    return result\n\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\nphi_mod = euler_totient(mod)\narray_size = n + 5\nfactorials = [1] * (array_size + 1)\nfor i in range(1, array_size + 1):\n    factorials[i] = (i * factorials[i - 1]) % mod\n\nif n <= 3:\n    print(0)\nelse:\n    dp = [0] * 2000\n    dp[0], dp[1], dp[2], dp[3] = 1, 2, 2, 1\n    seg_tree = build_segment_tree(2005)\n    for i in range(4):\n        update_segment(seg_tree, i, dp[i])\n    max_index = 3\n    total = 0\n    for iteration in range(n - 3):\n        prev_dp = dp[:]\n        partial_sum = 0\n        for j in range(iteration + 3):\n            for k in range(1, max_index + 2):\n                count = range_query(seg_tree, j + k + 1, 2004)\n                partial_sum = (partial_sum + count * prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + prev_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                update_segment(seg_tree, j + k, dp[j + k])\n        max_index += iteration + 3\n        product = modular_product(iteration + 4, n, mod)\n        total = (total + product * partial_sum) % mod\n    print(total)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] firstLine = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[0]);\n        int mod = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[1]);\n        \n        int phi_mod = eulerTotient(mod);\n        int arraySize = n + 5;\n        long[] factorials = new long[arraySize + 1];\n        factorials[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= arraySize; i++) {\n            factorials[i] = (i * factorials[i - 1]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        if (n <= 3) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n        } else {\n            long[] dp = new long[2000];\n            dp[0] = 1;\n            dp[1] = 2;\n            dp[2] = 2;\n            dp[3] = 1;\n            \n            int[] segTree = buildSegmentTree(2005);\n            for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n                updateSegment(segTree, i, (int)dp[i]);\n            }\n            \n            int maxIndex = 3;\n            long total = 0;\n            \n            for (int iteration = 0; iteration < n - 3; iteration++) {\n                long[] prevDp = dp.clone();\n                long partialSum = 0;\n                \n                for (int j = 0; j < iteration + 3; j++) {\n                    for (int k = 1; k <= maxIndex + 2; k++) {\n                        int count = rangeQuery(segTree, j + k + 1, 2004);\n                        partialSum = (partialSum + count * prevDp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                        dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + prevDp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                        updateSegment(segTree, j + k, (int)dp[j + k]);\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                maxIndex += iteration + 3;\n                long product = modularProduct(iteration + 4, n, mod);\n                total = (total + product * partialSum) % mod;\n            }\n            \n            System.out.println(total);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static int[] buildSegmentTree(int size) {\n        int treeSize = 1;\n        while (treeSize < size) {\n            treeSize *= 2;\n        }\n        return new int[treeSize * 2];\n    }\n    \n    private static void updateSegment(int[] tree, int index, int value) {\n        int pos = index + tree.length / 2;\n        tree[pos] = value;\n        pos /= 2;\n        while (pos > 0) {\n            tree[pos] = tree[pos * 2] + tree[pos * 2 + 1];\n            pos /= 2;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static int rangeQuery(int[] tree, int left, int right) {\n        left += tree.length / 2;\n        right += tree.length / 2;\n        int total = 0;\n        while (left <= right) {\n            if (left % 2 == 1) {\n                total += tree[left];\n                left += 1;\n            }\n            if (right % 2 == 0) {\n                total += tree[right];\n                right -= 1;\n            }\n            left /= 2;\n            right /= 2;\n        }\n        return total;\n    }\n    \n    private static List<Integer> primeFactors(int n) {\n        List<Integer> factors = new ArrayList<>();\n        int d = 2;\n        while (d * d <= n) {\n            while (n % d == 0) {\n                factors.add(d);\n                n /= d;\n            }\n            d += 1;\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            factors.add(n);\n        }\n        return factors;\n    }\n    \n    private static int eulerTotient(int n) {\n        List<Integer> factors = new ArrayList<>(new HashSet<>(primeFactors(n)));\n        int result = n;\n        for (int p : factors) {\n            result = result / p * (p - 1);\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n    \n    private static long modularProduct(int start, int end, int modulus) {\n        long result = 1;\n        for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {\n            result = (result * i) % modulus;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.987976616481319e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0001472126314183697, -2.8490614567999728e-05, -0.5759609937667847, -0.003522859187796712, -6.079655122448457e-06, -6.6756979322235566e-06, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -0.002227446297183633, -3.933898824470816e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.40932747349143e-05, -0.31326723098754883, -0.0006282739923335612, -0.4477626085281372, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.008840586990118027, -5.125986263010418e-06, -3.099436753473128e-0